%% W3D2 — Context Compression — Request-to-Response Sequence
%% Shows query-aware compression pipeline before each LLM call
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant App as Application
    participant Retriever as Retrieval Layer
    participant Router as Segment Router
    participant Compressor as Compressor Registry
    participant Assembler as Context Assembler
    participant LLM as LLM API

    User->>App: Submit query
    App->>Retriever: Fetch context segments\n(history, docs, tool outputs)
    Retriever-->>App: Raw segments\n(avg 8,000–12,000 tokens)

    App->>Router: Route segments with query
    Router->>Router: Score each segment\nagainst query (relevance 0–1)

    alt Segment tokens < 500 (below threshold)
        Router-->>Assembler: Pass segment uncompressed
    else Segment tokens >= 500
        Router->>Compressor: Dispatch with type + budget
        Note over Compressor: History → Abstractive\nDocuments → Extractive\nTool output → Token-level
        Compressor->>Compressor: Apply query-aware compression
        Compressor-->>Assembler: Compressed segment
    end

    Note over Assembler: System prompt always\nbypasses compression
    Assembler->>Assembler: Concatenate in fixed order:\nsystem → history → docs → tools
    Assembler-->>App: Compressed context\n(avg 2,000–3,000 tokens)

    App->>LLM: Compressed context + query
    LLM-->>App: Completion response
    App-->>User: Final answer
